## Genome naming and metadata

The current version of RECAP-PROK Module 3 includes predefined genome names corresponding to the bacterial and plasmid genomes used in the original case study dataset.

These names are stored in the GENOME_NAMES metadata section of the CDS mapping interpretation script and are used only for:

- output table descriptions
- figure labels
- visualization purposes

The genome names are not used for CDS mapping, Liftoff annotation transfer, CDS classification, or any numerical calculation.

For applying this workflow to a different bacterial community or genome set, the metadata labels should be adapted to match the user's own genome identifiers.
This can be done by updating the genome metadata section before running the workflow.

The input genome files should be provided according to the Galaxy tool input requirements. Users do not need to modify the analysis scripts for the original case study dataset.
